				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Simplify ProviderRegistration module structure\n\nRemove extensive header documentation and flatten the `ProviderRegistration` module hierarchy in `ApplicationState`. Replace the previous dual-module pattern (`mod.rs` re-exporting `ProviderRegistration.rs`) with a single canonical path where the struct resides in `ProviderRegistration/ProviderRegistration.rs`.\n\nThis aligns with the ongoing decomposition of `ExtensionState` into file-per-struct PascalCase modules, ensuring consistent symbol resolution for the `Registration` DTO used by the gRPC `Vine` protocol handlers.",
			"SHA": "dcea36c734da4254b4c6750a1be2dd09fc551e6c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T05:44:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1003,
				8
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose Terminal RPC handlers into file-per-struct modules\n\nExtract all gRPC entry points within `Source/RPC/CocoonService/Terminal` into dedicated PascalCase modules to align with the project-wide architectural convention. New modules cover the full terminal lifecycle: `OpenTerminal` (spawning PTY via `TerminalProvider::CreateTerminal`), `CloseTerminal` (disposing via `DisposeTerminal`), `TerminalInput` (forwarding bytes to the master writer), `ResizeTerminal` (emitting dimensions to Sky), and notifications for `AcceptTerminalOpened`, `AcceptTerminalClosed`, `AcceptTerminalProcessData`, and `AcceptTerminalProcessId`.\n\nEach handler implements the `Fn` signature required for Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro and bridges the `Vine` gRPC protocol to the `Sky` UI layer. Notifications are emitted via Tauri events (`sky://terminal/create`, `/exit`, `/data`, `/processId`, `/resize`) using lossy UTF-8 decoding for stream data. This completes the decomposition of the `CocoonService` namespace, ensuring consistent symbol resolution and maintainability across the terminal subsystem.",
			"SHA": "1a89bda0e090338927fd29676be62533ef50ca16"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T05:43:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				994,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Decompose TreeView RPC handlers into file-per-struct modules\n\nExtract the `TreeView` gRPC entry points within `Source/RPC/CocoonService` into dedicated PascalCase modules (`EnqueueTreeViewEmit`, `GetTreeChildren`, `RegisterTreeViewProvider`, `ViewIdHandle`) to align with the project-wide architectural convention.\n\nThe `EnqueueTreeViewEmit` module implements a static batcher that coalesces 30+ `tree-view/create` events from boot into single 16 ms window payloads, utilizing `AtomicBool` locking and `tokio::spawn` for non-blocking emission to the `Sky` UI layer. `GetTreeChildren` bridges the `Vine` gRPC protocol to the `Cocoon` extension host, performing a 5-second timeout-protected round-trip to `$provideTreeChildren` and returning empty lists on provider registration failures. `RegisterTreeViewProvider` registers tree data providers in `ApplicationState` using a consistent 31-based string hash for handle generation and triggers the batched emit. `ViewIdHandle` centralizes the hash logic for provider lookup.\n\nAll handlers are exposed as `Fn` functions for invocation via `Tauri::generate_handler!`, completing the refactoring of the `CocoonService` RPC namespace.",
			"SHA": "39923726563a05fc656a7c3766fa7bd4f9232528"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T05:42:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				989,
				16
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Decompose Window RPC handlers into file-per-struct modules\n\nExtract all gRPC entry points within the `Source/RPC/CocoonService/Window` namespace into dedicated PascalCase modules. This completes the architectural refactor initiated in previous commits for Workspace, Command, and Configuration, ensuring the monolithic `mod.rs` no longer contains inline handler logic.\n\nNew modules include handlers for window management (CreateWebviewPanel, DisposeWebviewPanel, SetWebviewHtml), status bar operations (CreateStatusBarItem, SetStatusBarText), and user interface interactions (ShowErrorMessage, ShowInformationMessage, ShowWarningMessage, ShowInputBox, ShowQuickPick, ShowTextDocument). Additional handlers cover progress reporting (ShowProgress, ReportProgress) and webview messaging (OnDidReceiveMessage, PostWebviewMessage).\n\nEach handler implements the `Fn` signature required by Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro and bridges the `Vine` gRPC protocol to the `Sky` UI layer. The implementations utilize the `CommonLibrary` traits (`StatusBarProvider`, `WebviewProvider`, `UserInterfaceProvider`) for state registration and stateful operations. Fallback mechanisms via direct `sky://` Tauri events are preserved for trait failures to prevent state leaks in webview and status bar components.",
			"SHA": "adfab9f41833191c1652fc00fb0b0d91aa16054d"
		}
	],
